course: dictionary
lesson: 14795
title: The punchline
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A joke is often a short story with a funny ending. The punchline is the last line or words of the joke, the part that makes it funny. «Wait for the punchline!» means wait for the ending that makes the joke funny.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Sam told a joke, but he forgot the punchline.» A joke needs its funny ending to work, so punchline must mean the funny last part. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "Sam forgot the funny last part" still makes sense.
explain: The word can also mean the surprising or important ending of a story, speech or advert. «The advert ended with a clever punchline that made everyone laugh.» Comedians practise timing the punchline, so it lands at the right moment.
fact: A punchline is the last line or words of a joke.
fact: The punchline is the part that makes a joke funny.
fact: «Punchline» can also mean the surprising or important ending of a story, speech or advert.
fact: Comedians practise timing the punchline, so that it gets the laugh at the right moment.
fact: Useful phrases: «deliver the punchline», «get the punchline», «forget the punchline».
exercise: «Wait for the punchline!» What is a punchline? | The first line of a story | *The last line of a joke, which makes it funny | A type of sports shoe | A loud noise made by a punch
exercise: «Sam told a joke, but he forgot the punchline.» What did Sam forget? | The time of the bus | *The funny last part of the joke | His coat for the trip | The name of the school
exercise: «The advert ended with a clever punchline that made everyone laugh.» Find and copy one word that means the ending that makes people laugh. | *punchline | ended | advert | clever
test: «The advert ended with a clever punchline that made everyone laugh.» What made everyone laugh? | The colour of the car | The music at the start | *The punchline at the end | The price of the shoes
test: What does punchline mean in a speech? | The opening greeting | *The surprising or important ending | The loudest word | The name of the speaker
exam: Why do comedians practise the timing of the punchline? | So the joke is made longer | So it can be forgotten on stage | So it is said as quietly as possible | *So it lands at the right moment and gets the laugh
